        "header": "2Harness Design",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.26860/2610.26860v1/architecture.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Overview of OpenVLHarness.The MLLM orchestrator invokes capabilities through typed interfaces. The capability layer connects these interfaces to underlying models and services and renders their outputs into model-facing evidence: here, a labeled mask overlay accompanied by a textual description and normalized bounding boxes. Persistent multimodal memory retains image artifacts, structured data, and web references under reusable handles. An Environment Update advertises the available artifacts to the orchestrator, allowing subsequent calls to reuse earlier evidence, including through memory-grounded computation.",
                "position": 532
            },
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.26860/2610.26860v1/qualitative_examples.png",
                "caption": "Figure 3:Qualitative examples of OpenVLHarness.(a)Camera poses, depth, and grounding are combined in code to measure a 3D distance (ExampleF).(b)Grounded crops are passed to OCR and image search, and the answer is verified on the web (ExampleF).(c)Masks from two grounding queries are reconciled in code to reach the exact count (ExampleF).",
                "position": 609
            }
        ]
    },
